<%
  var S = canada.SOURCES;
  var pageUrl = siteUrl + '/how-to-calculate-gst-on-canadian-invoices';
  var faqs = [
    ['How do I calculate GST on a $1,000 invoice?', 'Multiply the amount before tax by the rate. At 5% GST: 1,000 x 0.05 = $50, total $1,050. In Ontario (13% HST): $130 tax, total $1,130. In British Columbia: $50 GST plus $70 PST, total $1,120.'],
    ['Which province has the highest sales tax?', 'New Brunswick, Newfoundland and Labrador and Prince Edward Island have the highest rate: 15% HST. Quebec follows at 14.975% combined (5% GST + 9.975% QST), then Nova Scotia at 14% HST. Alberta and the three territories charge only the 5% GST.'],
    ['What is the HST rate in Nova Scotia in 2026?', '14%. Nova Scotia lowered its HST from 15% to 14% on 1 April 2025, and the CRA rate table still shows 14% as of ' + canada.RATES_CHECKED + '. Update any invoice template that still uses 15%.'],
    ['Is PST or QST charged on top of the GST?', 'No. GST and the provincial tax are each calculated on the price before tax. On $100 in Quebec you charge $5.00 GST and $9.98 QST (9.975%), not QST on $105.'],
    ['Do I show the federal and provincial parts of HST separately?', 'No. The CRA says that where HST applies you show the total HST rate as one line and do not split it into federal and provincial parts.'],
    ['Do I have to charge GST/HST if my business is small?', 'Not if you are a small supplier: worldwide taxable sales of $30,000 or less over four consecutive calendar quarters. Once you pass that amount you must register and charge GST/HST. If you are not registered, do not charge GST/HST on your invoices.'],
    ['What does a GST/HST registration number look like?', 'Your 9-digit business number followed by RT and a 4-digit account number, for example 123456789 RT0001. A Quebec QST number looks like 1234567890 TQ0001.']
  ];
%><!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>How to Calculate GST on Canadian Invoices (2026 Rates)</title>
<meta name="description" content="Multiply the pre-tax amount by your province's rate: 5% GST, 13-15% HST, or GST plus PST/QST. Rates checked Oct 2026, worked examples, calculator, CRA invoice rules.">
