<body>
<%- include('partials/nav') %>
<div class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> › <a href="/free-invoice-generator-canada">Canada</a> › GST on invoices</div>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="in">
    <h1>How to Calculate GST on Canadian Invoices</h1>
    <p class="lede">Multiply the amount before tax by the rate for your client's province, put each tax on its own line, and add it to the subtotal. Rates below were last checked on <%= canada.RATES_CHECKED %>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="wrap prose">
  <div class="answer">
    <p><strong>The short answer:</strong> GST = amount before tax x 5%. In Ontario, Nova Scotia, New Brunswick, Newfoundland and Labrador and PEI you charge one HST line instead (13%, 14% or 15%). In British Columbia, Saskatchewan, Manitoba and Quebec you charge 5% GST plus the provincial tax (PST, RST or QST), each worked out on the price before tax and shown on its own line.</p>
    <p><strong>Example:</strong> $1,000 of work for an Ontario client: 1,000 x 13% = $130 HST, invoice total $1,130.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="calc" aria-labelledby="calcH">
    <h2 id="calcH">GST/HST calculator</h2>
    <p class="sub">Pick the province, enter the amount, and get the lines to put on the invoice.</p>
    <div class="row">
      <div><label for="cProv">Province or territory</label>
        <select id="cProv">
          <% canada.PROVINCES.forEach(function(p){ %><option value="<%= p.code %>"<%= p.code === 'ON' ? ' selected' : '' %>><%= p.name %> (<%= p.summary %>)</option><% }) %>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div><label for="cAmt">Amount (CAD)</label><input type="number" id="cAmt" value="1000" min="0" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal"></div>
      <div><label for="cMode">The amount is</label>
        <select id="cMode"><option value="add">before tax</option><option value="remove">tax included</option></select>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="res" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="line"><span>Amount before tax</span><span id="rSub"></span></div>
      <div id="rLines"></div>
      <div class="line total"><span>Invoice total</span><span id="rTot"></span></div>
      <div class="how" id="rHow"></div>
    </div>
    <a class="btn" id="cGo" href="/free-invoice-generator-canada?province=ON&amount=1000">Create this invoice with these tax lines</a>
  </section>

  <h2>The formula for each type of province</h2>
  <h3>GST only: Alberta, Yukon, Northwest Territories, Nunavut</h3>
  <div class="formula">GST = amount before tax x 0.05<br>Total = amount + GST<br><b>$800 x 0.05 = $40 GST, total $840</b></div>
  <h3>HST: Ontario, Nova Scotia, New Brunswick, Newfoundland and Labrador, PEI</h3>
  <div class="formula">HST = amount before tax x HST rate (0.13, 0.14 or 0.15)<br>Total = amount + HST<br><b>$2,500 x 0.13 = $325 HST, total $2,825</b></div>
  <h3>GST + provincial tax: British Columbia, Saskatchewan, Manitoba, Quebec</h3>
  <div class="formula">GST = amount x 0.05<br>PST / RST / QST = amount x provincial rate   (not on the GST)<br>Total = amount + GST + provincial tax<br><b>BC: $1,500 x 0.05 = $75 GST, $1,500 x 0.07 = $105 PST, total $1,680</b></div>
  <h3>Working backwards from a tax-included total</h3>
  <div class="formula">Amount before tax = total / (1 + total rate)<br>Tax = total minus amount before tax<br><b>Ontario: $1,130 / 1.13 = $1,000, so HST = $130</b></div>

  <h2 id="rates">GST, HST and PST rates by province (2026)</h2>
  <table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th>Province or territory</th><th>Lines on the invoice</th><th class="num">GST / HST</th><th class="num">Provincial tax</th><th class="num">Total</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <% canada.PROVINCES.forEach(function(p){ var pp = provinces.filter(function(x){ return x.code === p.code; })[0]; %>
      <tr>
        <td class="strong"><% if (pp) { %><a href="/<%= pp.slug %>"><%= p.name %></a><% } else { %><%= p.name %><% } %></td>
        <td><%= p.type === 'HST' ? 'HST (one line)' : p.type === 'GST' ? 'GST' : 'GST + ' + p.pstName %></td>
        <td class="num"><%= p.type === 'HST' ? p.hst + '% HST' : '5% GST' %></td>
        <td class="num"><%= p.type === 'GST+PST' ? p.pst + '% ' + p.pstName : '-' %></td>
        <td class="num strong"><%= p.total %>%<%= p.note ? '*' : '' %></td>
      </tr>
      <% }) %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="source">* Nova Scotia's HST fell from 15% to 14% on 1 April 2025. Last checked <%= canada.RATES_CHECKED %> against the <a href="<%= S.cra.url %>" rel="noopener">CRA GST/HST rates table</a> and <a href="<%= S.craCharge.url %>" rel="noopener">which rate to charge</a>, <a href="<%= S.bc.url %>" rel="noopener">BC PST</a>, <a href="<%= S.sk.url %>" rel="noopener">Saskatchewan PST</a>, <a href="<%= S.mb.url %>" rel="noopener">Manitoba RST</a> and <a href="<%= S.qc.url %>" rel="noopener">Revenu Québec (QST)</a>. On that date the CRA table showed no other rate change since the Nova Scotia cut.</p>

  <h2>Worked examples</h2>
  <div class="example"><h3>Ontario: $2,500 web design project</h3><ol><li>Amount before tax: $2,500.00</li><li>HST 13%: 2,500 x 0.13 = $325.00</li><li>Total: $2,825.00, with one line "HST (13%)"</li></ol></div>
  <div class="example"><h3>Nova Scotia: $1,200 of consulting</h3><ol><li>Amount before tax: $1,200.00</li><li>HST 14%: 1,200 x 0.14 = $168.00 (at the old 15% it would have been $180.00)</li><li>Total: $1,368.00</li></ol></div>
  <div class="example"><h3>British Columbia: $1,500 of taxable goods</h3><ol><li>Amount before tax: $1,500.00</li><li>GST 5%: $75.00</li><li>PST 7% on the $1,500 (not on the GST): $105.00</li><li>Total: $1,680.00, with GST and PST on separate lines</li></ol></div>
  <div class="example"><h3>Quebec: $4,000 of services</h3><ol><li>Amount before tax: $4,000.00</li><li>GST 5%: $200.00</li><li>QST 9.975% on the $4,000: $399.00</li><li>Total: $4,599.00. Show GST and QST separately with both registration numbers.</li></ol></div>
  <div class="example"><h3>Alberta: $800 repair job</h3><ol><li>Amount before tax: $800.00</li><li>GST 5%: $40.00</li><li>Total: $840.00. No provincial sales tax in Alberta.</li></ol></div>

  <h2>Which province's rate do you charge?</h2>
  <p>The rate depends on the <strong>place of supply</strong>, not on where your business is based. The CRA's general rules:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Goods</strong> are supplied in the province where you deliver them or make them available, or the province you ship them to.</li>
    <li><strong>Services</strong> are generally supplied in the province of your client's address, when you get that address in the normal course of business.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>So a GST/HST-registered consultant in Alberta who bills a client in Toronto charges 13% HST, not Alberta's 5%. There are special rules for some services (for example, services related to real property or passenger transport). See the <a href="<%= S.craPlace.url %>" rel="noopener">CRA place of supply rules</a>.</p>
  <p>Provincial sales taxes (BC PST, Saskatchewan PST, Manitoba RST, Quebec QST) are run by the provinces. Whether you must register and collect them depends on that province's rules, so check the provincial site linked in the source note above before adding a PST line.</p>

  <h2 id="invoice">What the CRA requires on the invoice</h2>
  <p>Your client needs certain details on the invoice to claim input tax credits (ITCs). The list depends on the total amount of the sale:</p>
  <table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th>Total sale</th><th>Information required</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td class="strong">Under $100</td><td>Your business or trading name; the invoice date (or the date the tax was paid or payable if there is no invoice); the total amount paid or payable.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="strong">$100 to $499.99</td><td>All of the above, plus your <strong>GST/HST registration number</strong>; the total GST/HST charged, or a statement that the price includes GST/HST at the applicable rate; and, if the invoice mixes taxable and exempt items, which is which.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="strong">$500 or more</td><td>All of the above, plus the <strong>buyer's name</strong> (or trading name or authorized agent), a <strong>brief description</strong> of the goods or services, and the <strong>terms of payment</strong>.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="source">Source: <a href="<%= S.craItc.url %>" rel="noopener">CRA, input tax credits: documents and information required</a>. Checked <%= canada.RATES_CHECKED %>.</p>
  <p>How to show the tax:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>HST provinces:</strong> one line with the total HST rate, for example "HST (13%)". The CRA says not to show the federal and provincial parts separately.</li>
    <li><strong>GST + PST provinces:</strong> GST and the provincial tax on separate lines, each with its rate.</li>
    <li><strong>Quebec:</strong> GST (5%) and QST (9.975%) on separate lines. Revenu Québec says combined rates such as 14.975% must not appear on the invoice.</li>
    <li><strong>Registration numbers:</strong> GST/HST numbers are your 9-digit business number + RT + 4 digits, for example <code>123456789 RT0001</code> (<a href="<%= S.rc4022.url %>" rel="noopener">CRA RC4022</a>). QST numbers look like <code>1234567890 TQ0001</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Example: an Ontario invoice that meets the $500+ requirements</h3>
  <div class="inv" role="img" aria-label="Sample Ontario invoice with HST">
    <div class="top">
      <div><div style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700;color:var(--blue)">INVOICE</div><div class="k">No. INV-2026-041, <span class="mark">date 6 October 2026</span></div></div>
      <div style="text-align:right;line-height:1.5"><strong class="mark">Birch Lane Studio</strong><br>45 Queen St W, Toronto ON<br><span class="mark">GST/HST no. 123456789 RT0001</span></div>
    </div>
    <div><div class="k">Bill to</div><strong class="mark">Northern Goods Inc.</strong>, 200 Bay St, Toronto ON</div>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Description</th><th class="r">Amount</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="mark">Website redesign, phase 1 (design and build)</td><td class="r">2,500.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Subtotal</td><td class="r">2,500.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mark">HST (13%)</td><td class="r">325.00</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Total due</strong></td><td class="r"><strong class="mark">2,825.00</strong></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <div class="k" style="text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:12.5px"><span class="mark">Terms: due within 14 days (20 October 2026)</span> by e-transfer to accounts@birchlane.example</div>
  </div>
  <p class="source">Highlighted: the items the CRA lists for a sale of $500 or more. Names and numbers are made up.</p>

  <h2>Do you have to charge GST/HST at all?</h2>
  <p>You must register for and charge GST/HST once your worldwide taxable sales go over <strong>$30,000</strong> in a single calendar quarter or over the last four consecutive calendar quarters. Below that you are a <strong>small supplier</strong> and registration is optional. If you are not registered, do not put GST/HST on your invoices. Source: <a href="<%= S.craRegister.url %>" rel="noopener">CRA, when to register and start charging the GST/HST</a>.</p>

  <h2>Clients outside Canada</h2>
  <p>Many exports of goods, and some services supplied to non-residents, are <strong>zero-rated</strong>: taxable at 0%, so no GST/HST is charged, while you can still claim input tax credits. Whether your service qualifies depends on what it is and where it is used, so check the <a href="<%= S.craExports.url %>" rel="noopener">CRA guidance on exports</a> before you leave the tax off.</p>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Still charging 15% in Nova Scotia.</strong> The rate is 14% for tax that becomes payable on or after 1 April 2025.</li>
    <li><strong>Charging PST or QST on the GST.</strong> Each tax is worked out on the price before tax.</li>
    <li><strong>Splitting HST</strong> into "GST 5% + provincial 8%". Show one HST line.</li>
    <li><strong>Using your own province's rate</strong> instead of the place of supply (usually your client's province for services).</li>
    <li><strong>No GST/HST number</strong> on an invoice of $100 or more. Registered clients will ask you to reissue it before they pay.</li>
    <li><strong>Rounding each line differently.</strong> Work out each tax on the subtotal and round once to the nearest cent.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="cta-band">
    <h2>Make the invoice with the right tax lines</h2>
    <p>Pick the province and the GST, HST, PST or QST lines fill in at the rates above. Free PDF, no signup.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="/free-invoice-generator-canada">Open the Canadian invoice generator</a>
  </div>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <div class="faq">
    <% faqs.forEach(function(f){ %><details><summary><%= f[0] %></summary><p><%= f[1] %></p></details><% }) %>
  </div>

  <h2>Province calculators</h2>
  <ul class="linklist">
    <% provinces.forEach(function(p){ %><li><a href="/<%= p.slug %>"><%= p.name %>: <%= p.system %> <%= p.combined %>%</a></li><% }) %>
    <li><a href="/free-invoice-generator-canada">Canadian invoice generator</a></li>
    <li><a href="/blog/gst-invoice-guide">GST invoices in Australia, India, Canada and Singapore</a></li>
  </ul>
</div>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
<script>
(function(){
  var P=<%- JSON.stringify(canada.PROVINCES.map(function(p){ return { code: p.code, taxes: p.taxes }; })) %>;
  var $=function(i){return document.getElementById(i);};
  function f(n){return '$'+n.toLocaleString('en-CA',{minimumFractionDigits:2,maximumFractionDigits:2});}
  function calc(){
    var p=P.filter(function(x){return x.code===$('cProv').value;})[0];
    var amt=parseFloat($('cAmt').value)||0, mode=$('cMode').value;
    var rate=p.taxes.reduce(function(a,t){return a+t.rate;},0);
    var base=mode==='add'?amt:amt/(1+rate/100);
    base=Math.round(base*100)/100;
    var lines=p.taxes.map(function(t){return {label:t.label,rate:t.rate,amount:Math.round(base*t.rate)/100};});
    var tot=base+lines.reduce(function(a,l){return a+l.amount;},0);
    $('rSub').textContent=f(base);
    $('rLines').innerHTML=lines.map(function(l){return '<div class="line"><span>'+l.label+' ('+l.rate+'%)</span><span>'+f(l.amount)+'</span></div>';}).join('');
    $('rTot').textContent=f(tot);
    $('rHow').textContent=lines.map(function(l){return l.label+' = '+base.toFixed(2)+' x '+(l.rate/100)+' = '+l.amount.toFixed(2);}).join(';  ');
    $('cGo').href='/free-invoice-generator-canada?province='+p.code+'&amount='+base.toFixed(2);
  }
  ['cProv','cAmt','cMode'].forEach(function(id){$(id).addEventListener('input',calc);$(id).addEventListener('change',calc);});
  calc();
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
